<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33130" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ossa</span></b> , ae, f. (m., <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 1,
		155</span></i>), = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὄσσα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a high mountain in
				Thessaly</i>, now <i>Kissovo</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 3,
			2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 8, 15, § 30</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ter sunt conati imponere Pelio Ossam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 1, 281</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ossan,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					1, 307</span></i>
			.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ossaeus</span></b> , a, um, adj., <i>Ossean</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saxa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg. Cir. 33</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rupes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					6, 334</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">media,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 2, 82</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ossaei bimembres,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the Centaurs who dwell about Ossa</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 12, 554</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
